    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0259" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">651.113/120a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France
                        (Straus)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-05-13T14:00:00-04:00">May 13, 1933—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. This morning’s <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> reports that
                    France has completed an agreement with the Italians<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d110-f1"/> similar to the Belgian agreement<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d110-f2"/> which removes from Italian products imported into France
                    the French turnover tax. You will recall that at the time of the Franco-Belgian
                    agreement we made representations to the effect that this discrimination should
                    be rectified particularly in respect of copper. American copper interests are
                    again pressing the Department with regard to this matter.</p>
                <p>You are requested to present a protest either orally or in writing, as you may
                    deem more appropriate, to the French Government, saying that this Government
                    cannot recognize this method of discrimination in favor <pb facs="0260" n="156"
                        xml:id="pg156"/> of third countries on the excuse that such preferential
                    treatment arises out of an effort on the part of France to avoid double
                    taxation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
